title: scene_faust
---
<<bg kosciol_normal>>

He wobbled farther inside without really looking forward.
Ariel bumped into something warm…
He bumped into someone's chest.  

<<show ariel basic right>>
<<show faust basic left>>

Ariel stepped away from the person he just bumped into.
The person in front of him was probably the same one mentioned by the church.
The priest Ariel was supposed to help.

He looked tired and slightly annoyed, but at least not mad.
-> Forgive me, Father. I didn't see you.
   Father: Don't worry, it's nothing.
   Father: You must be the priest who was supposed to be sent to me, mustn't you?
-> I'm sorry handsome… I mean Father… hot Father
   // <<show faust annoyed left>>
   Father:...
   Father: Who are you?
   Father: Are you the Priest?
   //<<show faust basic left>>
-> I’m so sorry… I didn't mean to bump into you, Father. Forgive me.
   Father: Don't worry, it's nothing.
   Father: You must be the priest who was supposed to be sent to me, mustn't you?

Ariel: Yes, I am…
Ariel: And I'm ready to help but I'm not entirely sure what the situation in the city is and how I can be of assistance…

Father: You've probably heard about the invasion of demonic energy.
Father: The city is festering with it and the people think only about the physical aspects of love.
Father: As the Creator’s envoys, the commissionaires of Love, it is our duty to convert them to the side of righteousness.
Father: It’s not an easy task to handle but I was informed of your outstanding performance during your seminaries.
Father: I was hoping that wasn’t just idle chatter, but now that I look at you…
Father: Well, let’s say my doubts were right.

Ariel seems scared.
It’s true he was doing well in school, but he never really had to perform an actual exorcism alone.
All those times he had a back up, someone to help him and be there at all times, but this person doesn’t seem very eager to help. 

Ariel looked at the handsome priest.
-> Thanks hottie.
	// <<show faust annoyed left>>
	Father: Don't call me that.
	Ariel: Okay, sure… so, how can we convert them?
	Father: Well, you can always talk to them, but it's not very effective.
-> Thank you Father. How can we convert them?
	Father: Well, you can always talk to them, but it's not very effective.

	Father: It's better to perform an exorcism every day but I'm too old to do this alone.

Ariel: Are you talking about standard exorcism?
Ariel: I think I can do that, Father.

Father: Don't be so sure.
Father: And don’t be late. 

Ariel: Well, I won’t be late if you give me the time.

The other priest seems to be a little bit fed up with Ariel.
Maybe he expected someone more adept than a newbie with no real experience.  

Father: Meet me tomorrow afternoon.
Father: Now go.

Ariel walked towards the exit, but stopped halfway and looked back at the other priest once again.
Ariel: May I at least know your name, Father?
Ariel: By the way, my name is Ariel…

Father: I know, child, the Great Church sent me your portfolio.
Father: My name is Faust.
Faust: Father Faust to you.

Ariel: Sure.
Ariel smiled gently and finally left the church.

<<hide Faust>>
<<hide Ariel>>

The air outside of it felt lighter than the one in town, as if the church itself was protecting them from the surrounding sin.
Ariel took a deep breath, a shiver ran through his skin.
The seriousness of the task hit him now like a train.
What if he’s not prepared?
What if he’s going to fail?
The pureness of those souls are in his hands, it's his responsibility to help them.
To calm himself down he decided to explore the nearby area a little bit to get a better idea of the place. 

<<jump scene_marcin>>
===
